   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Comic Panels\n\nThe frame cracks into a three-panel comic page with speed lines and halftone, then the action panel bursts into a full-frame word such as POW. A built-in lockup stands in for the hero; a host replaces the contents of the .cp-hero layer with its own logo or headline.\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 2.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A logo, product or headline should land with comic-book energy, framed in a hero panel with speed lines.\n- A playful launch or social clip needs a loud sound-effect beat, like POW, ZAP or NEW, that takes over the frame.\n- The scene should turn from a single hero shot into a page layout in one move.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You only need the manga-style impact lines around an element, without the page: use speed-lines.\n- The hit should be a heavy slam with a camera jolt rather than a page cracking: use impact-shake.\n- The burst should be a sculptural ribbon opener rather than a printed comic page: use radial-burst.\n\nVariables:\n- word (string): Word, default \"POW\"\n- hero_text (string): Hero text, default \"Your brand\"\n- hero_scale (number, 0.3-1): Hero scale, default 0.62\n- ink (color): Ink, default \"#111111\"\n- paper (color): Paper, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- accent (color): Accent, default \"#E5322D\"\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Comic Panels\n\n  The frame cracks into a three-panel comic page with speed lines and halftone, then the action panel bursts into a full-frame word. The built-in hero lockup (a rounded icon and a line of text) is a stand-in: a host puts its own logo or headline in by replacing the contents of the .cp-hero layer.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/comic-panels/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"comic-panels\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"word\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Word\", \"description\": \"Word in the starburst, such as POW. Leave empty for no word.\", \"default\": \"POW\"},\n    {\"id\": \"hero_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Hero text\", \"description\": \"Text of the built-in hero lockup.\", \"default\": \"Your brand\"},\n    {\"id\": \"hero_scale\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Hero scale\", \"description\": \"Scale of the hero inside the top panel.\", \"default\": 0.62, \"min\": 0.3, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.02},\n    {\"id\": \"ink\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Ink\", \"description\": \"Ink color.\", \"default\": \"#111111\"},\n    {\"id\": \"paper\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Paper\", \"description\": \"Paper color.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Accent\", \"description\": \"Accent color.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Comic Panels</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #ffffff; }\n        .cp-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }\n        .cp-stage > svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }\n        .cp-hero { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .cp-lockup { display: flex; align-items: center; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .cp-icon { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex: none; }\n        .cp-name { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"comic-panels\" data-duration=\"2.2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"cp-clip\" class=\"cp-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.2\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg id=\"cp-back\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n          <div id=\"cp-hero\" class=\"cp-hero\"><div class=\"cp-lockup\" id=\"cp-lockup\"><div class=\"cp-icon\" id=\"cp-icon\"><div id=\"cp-dot\"></div></div><span class=\"cp-name\" id=\"cp-name\"></span></div></div>\n          <svg id=\"cp-front\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n          <svg id=\"cp-top\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            var FPS = 30;\n            var W = root.clientWidth || 1080;\n            var H = root.clientHeight || 1920;\n\n            // Seeded random in [0, 1): a string hash, so the same key always gives the same value.\n            function rnd(key) {\n              var h = 1779033703 ^ key.length;\n              for (var i = 0; i < key.length; i++) {\n                h = Math.imul(h ^ key.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353);\n                h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909);\n              h ^= h >>> 16;\n              return (h >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n\n            // Piecewise-linear map of x from inR to outR, optionally eased per segment and clamped.\n            function interp(x, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var i = 0;\n              if (x >= inR[n - 1]) i = n - 2;\n              else if (x > inR[0]) { while (x > inR[i + 1]) i++; }\n              var t = (x - inR[i]) / (inR[i + 1] - inR[i]);\n              if (o.clamp !== false) t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t));\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i] + (outR[i + 1] - outR[i]) * t;\n            }\n            function clamp01(t) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t)); }\n\n            // Easings with the usual names; every one maps 0..1 to 0..1.\n            var E = {\n              linear: function (t) { return t; },\n              quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n              cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n              sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n              back: function (s) { return function (t) { return t * t * ((s + 1) * t - s); }; },\n              out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n              inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; },\n              bezier: function (x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var k = 0; k < 24; k++) {\n                    var mt = 1 - t;\n                    var bx = 3 * mt * mt * t * x1 + 3 * mt * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (bx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var m = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * m * m * t * y1 + 3 * m * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n            };\n\n            function fmt(n) { return Math.round(n * 10) / 10; }\n\n            function dot(x, y, r) {\n              return \"M \" + fmt(x - r) + \" \" + fmt(y) + \" a \" + fmt(r) + \" \" + fmt(r) + \" 0 1 0 \" + fmt(r * 2) + \" 0 a \" + fmt(r) + \" \" + fmt(r) + \" 0 1 0 \" + fmt(-r * 2) + \" 0 \";\n            }\n\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function el(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            // Runs draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking to a time always draws the same picture.\n            function drive(frames, draw) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var word = typeof vars.word === \"string\" ? vars.word : \"POW\";\n            var heroText = str(vars.hero_text, \"Your brand\");\n            var heroScale = num(vars.hero_scale, 0.62, 0.3, 1);\n            var ink = str(vars.ink, \"#111111\"), paper = str(vars.paper, \"#FFFFFF\"), accent = str(vars.accent, \"#E5322D\");\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.1, 4);\n            root.style.background = paper;\n\n            var u = Math.min(W, H) / 720;\n            var FONT = \"'Arial Black', Impact, Inter, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif\";\n            function poly(points) { return points.map(function (p) { return p.join(\",\"); }).join(\" \"); }\n            var inOut = E.inOut(E.cubic), outCubic = E.out(E.cubic), outExp = E.out(function (t) { return Math.pow(2, 10 * (t - 1)); }), inCubic = E.cubic;\n            function ease(t, a, b, easing) { return interp(t, [a, b], [0, 1], { easing: easing || inOut }); }\n\n            // Page geometry: one slanted horizontal gutter, one slanted vertical one.\n            var a0 = 0.6 * H, a1 = 0.5 * H;\n            function yA(x) { return a0 + ((a1 - a0) * x) / W; }\n            var b0 = [0.53 * W, yA(0.53 * W)], b1 = [0.46 * W, H];\n            var gutter = 16 * u, border = 5 * u;\n            var left = [[0, a0], b0, b1, [0, H]], right = [b0, [W, a1], [W, H], b1];\n\n            // Hero lockup, sized in pixels at the frame's scale.\n            var lock = document.getElementById(\"cp-lockup\"), icon = document.getElementById(\"cp-icon\"), dotEl = document.getElementById(\"cp-dot\"), nameEl = document.getElementById(\"cp-name\");\n            lock.style.gap = 28 * u + \"px\";\n            icon.style.cssText += \";width:\" + 120 * u + \"px;height:\" + 120 * u + \"px;border-radius:\" + 32 * u + \"px;background:\" + accent;\n            dotEl.style.cssText = \"width:\" + 36 * u + \"px;height:\" + 36 * u + \"px;border-radius:50%;background:\" + ink;\n            nameEl.style.cssText += \";font-size:\" + 104 * u + \"px;color:\" + ink;\n            nameEl.textContent = heroText;\n            var hero = document.getElementById(\"cp-hero\");\n\n            function setBox(svg) { svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + W + \" \" + H); }\n            var back = document.getElementById(\"cp-back\"), front = document.getElementById(\"cp-front\"), top = document.getElementById(\"cp-top\");\n            [back, front, top].forEach(setBox);\n\n            // Speed lines.\n            var wedgeG = el(\"g\", { fill: ink }, back);\n            var wedgeEls = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < 56; i++) wedgeEls.push(el(\"polygon\", {}, wedgeG));\n\n            // Front: the two panels, gutters, margin.\n            var defs = el(\"defs\", {}, front);\n            el(\"polygon\", { points: poly(left) }, el(\"clipPath\", { id: \"cp-left\" }, defs));\n            el(\"polygon\", { points: poly(right) }, el(\"clipPath\", { id: \"cp-right\" }, defs));\n            var leftG = el(\"g\", { \"clip-path\": \"url(#cp-left)\" }, front);\n            var leftSlide = el(\"g\", { opacity: 0 }, leftG);\n            el(\"polygon\", { points: poly(left), fill: paper }, leftSlide);\n            var joltDots = el(\"g\", { fill: accent }, leftSlide);\n            var pitch = 20 * u, dotsD = \"\";\n            for (var y = a1 - pitch; y < H + pitch; y += pitch) {\n              for (var x = 0; x < b0[0] + pitch; x += pitch) {\n                var ox = (Math.round(y / pitch) % 2) * (pitch / 2);\n                var d = Math.hypot(x + ox, H - y) / Math.hypot(b0[0], H - a0);\n                var r = pitch * 0.5 * Math.max(0, Math.min(1, 1.15 - d));\n                if (r > 0.6 * u) dotsD += dot(x + ox, y, r);\n              }\n            }\n            el(\"path\", { d: dotsD }, joltDots);\n            var rightG = el(\"g\", { \"clip-path\": \"url(#cp-right)\" }, front);\n            var rightSlide = el(\"g\", { opacity: 0 }, rightG);\n            el(\"polygon\", { points: poly(right), fill: ink }, rightSlide);\n            var burstHolderA = el(\"g\", {}, rightSlide);\n            var gutters = [ink, paper].map(function (stroke, pass) {\n              var g = el(\"g\", { stroke: stroke, \"stroke-width\": pass === 0 ? gutter + border * 2 : gutter, \"stroke-linecap\": \"butt\" }, front);\n              return [el(\"line\", {}, g), el(\"line\", {}, g)];\n            });\n            el(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + -W + \" \" + -H + \" H \" + 2 * W + \" V \" + 2 * H + \" H \" + -W + \" Z M 0 0 V \" + H + \" H \" + W + \" V 0 Z\", fill: paper, \"fill-rule\": \"evenodd\" }, front);\n            var marginPath = front.lastChild;\n            var marginRect = el(\"rect\", { fill: \"none\", stroke: ink, \"stroke-width\": border }, front);\n\n            // The starburst, drawn twice: inside the right panel until it bursts, then on top of everything.\n            function starburst(spikes, outer, inner, seed) {\n              var points = [];\n              for (var i = 0; i < spikes * 2; i++) {\n                var a = (i / (spikes * 2)) * Math.PI * 2 + (rnd(seed + \"-a-\" + i) - 0.5) * 0.12;\n                var r = i % 2 === 0 ? outer * (0.82 + 0.18 * rnd(seed + \"-r-\" + i)) : inner * (0.9 + 0.1 * rnd(seed + \"-r-\" + i));\n                points.push([Math.cos(a) * r, Math.sin(a) * r]);\n              }\n              return poly(points);\n            }\n            var c3 = [(b0[0] + W + W + b1[0]) / 4, (b0[1] + a1 + H + H) / 4];\n            var outer = 0.4 * (H - a1);\n            var redPts = starburst(16, outer, outer * 0.68, \"comic-red\");\n            var whitePts = starburst(13, outer * 0.62, outer * 0.42, \"comic-white\");\n            function makeBurst(parent) {\n              var g = el(\"g\", {}, parent);\n              var red = el(\"polygon\", { points: redPts, fill: accent, stroke: ink, \"stroke-linejoin\": \"round\" }, g);\n              var white = el(\"polygon\", { points: whitePts, fill: paper, stroke: ink, \"stroke-linejoin\": \"round\" }, g);\n              var wordG = el(\"g\", { \"text-anchor\": \"middle\", \"dominant-baseline\": \"central\", \"font-family\": FONT, \"font-weight\": 900, \"font-size\": outer * 0.4 }, g);\n              if (word) {\n                el(\"text\", { x: outer * 0.03, y: outer * 0.03, fill: accent }, wordG).textContent = word;\n                el(\"text\", { fill: ink }, wordG).textContent = word;\n              }\n              return { g: g, red: red, white: white, word: wordG };\n            }\n            var burstA = makeBurst(burstHolderA);\n            var jolted = el(\"g\", {}, top);\n            var burstB = makeBurst(jolted);\n            function updateBurst(b, center, spin, redScale, whiteScale) {\n              b.g.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + center[0] + \" \" + center[1] + \") rotate(\" + spin + \")\");\n              b.red.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"scale(\" + redScale + \")\");\n              b.red.setAttribute(\"stroke-width\", (border * 0.8) / redScale);\n              b.white.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"scale(\" + whiteScale + \")\");\n              b.white.setAttribute(\"stroke-width\", (border * 0.8) / whiteScale);\n              b.word.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"scale(\" + whiteScale + \") rotate(-8)\");\n            }\n\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var t = frame * speed;\n              var margin = ease(t, 0, 8) * 22 * u;\n              var crackA = ease(t, 2, 10, outCubic), crackB = ease(t, 8, 14, outCubic);\n              var slide2 = ease(t, 10, 18, outExp), slide3 = ease(t, 13, 21, outExp);\n              var burst = ease(t, 23, 34, inCubic), settle = ease(t, 30, 36, outCubic);\n              var shaking = t >= 22 && t < 31;\n              var step = Math.floor(t / 2);\n              var shake = shaking ? [(rnd(\"comic-sx-\" + step) - 0.5) * 14 * u, (rnd(\"comic-sy-\" + step) - 0.5) * 14 * u] : [0, 0];\n              var jolt = \"translate(\" + shake[0] + \" \" + shake[1] + \")\";\n              var heroFocus = [W / 2, interp(crackA, [0, 1], [H / 2, 0.27 * H])];\n              var heroS = interp(crackA, [0, 1], [1, heroScale]);\n\n              // Speed lines: wedges from the hero focus, redrawn every 2 frames.\n              wedgeG.setAttribute(\"transform\", jolt);\n              for (var i = 0; i < 56; i++) {\n                var a = (i / 56) * Math.PI * 2 + (rnd(\"comic-w-\" + step + \"-\" + i) - 0.5) * 0.09;\n                var spread = 0.008 + 0.014 * rnd(\"comic-ws-\" + step + \"-\" + i);\n                var r0 = (0.3 + 0.12 * rnd(\"comic-wr-\" + step + \"-\" + i)) * W * heroS, r1 = W * 1.2;\n                var at = function (r, d) { return [heroFocus[0] + Math.cos(a + d) * r, heroFocus[1] + Math.sin(a + d) * r * 0.62]; };\n                wedgeEls[i].setAttribute(\"points\", poly([at(r0, 0), at(r1, -spread), at(r1, spread)]));\n              }\n              hero.style.transform = \"translate(\" + (heroFocus[0] - W / 2 + shake[0]) + \"px, \" + (heroFocus[1] - H / 2 + shake[1]) + \"px) scale(\" + heroS + \")\";\n\n              leftSlide.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + (slide2 - 1) * b0[0] + \" 0)\");\n              leftSlide.setAttribute(\"opacity\", slide2 > 0 ? 1 : 0);\n              joltDots.setAttribute(\"transform\", jolt);\n              rightSlide.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + (1 - slide3) * (W - b1[0]) + \" 0)\");\n              rightSlide.setAttribute(\"opacity\", slide3 > 0 ? 1 : 0);\n              burstHolderA.setAttribute(\"transform\", jolt);\n\n              var pulse = 1 + 0.04 * Math.sin(t * 1.4);\n              var center = [interp(burst, [0, 1], [c3[0], W / 2]), interp(burst, [0, 1], [c3[1], H / 2])];\n              var redScale = interp(burst, [0, 1], [1, 9]) * pulse;\n              var whiteScale = interp(burst, [0, 1], [1, (0.4 * Math.min(W, H)) / (outer * 0.62)]) * pulse * interp(settle, [0, 1], [1.08, 1]);\n              var spin = interp(burst, [0, 1], [0, 14]);\n              updateBurst(burstA, center, spin, redScale, whiteScale);\n              updateBurst(burstB, center, spin, redScale, whiteScale);\n              burstHolderA.setAttribute(\"display\", burst === 0 ? \"inline\" : \"none\");\n              jolted.setAttribute(\"display\", burst > 0 ? \"inline\" : \"none\");\n              jolted.setAttribute(\"transform\", jolt);\n\n              // Gutters: ink edges first, then the white channel on top.\n              gutters.forEach(function (pair) {\n                var l1 = pair[0], l2 = pair[1];\n                var x2 = -gutter + (W + 2 * gutter) * crackA;\n                l1.setAttribute(\"x1\", -gutter); l1.setAttribute(\"y1\", yA(-gutter)); l1.setAttribute(\"x2\", x2); l1.setAttribute(\"y2\", yA(x2));\n                l2.setAttribute(\"x1\", b0[0]); l2.setAttribute(\"y1\", b0[1]);\n                l2.setAttribute(\"x2\", b0[0] + (b1[0] + (b1[0] - b0[0]) * 0.05 - b0[0]) * crackB);\n                l2.setAttribute(\"y2\", b0[1] + (H * 1.05 - b0[1]) * crackB);\n              });\n              marginPath.setAttribute(\"d\", \"M \" + -W + \" \" + -H + \" H \" + 2 * W + \" V \" + 2 * H + \" H \" + -W + \" Z M \" + margin + \" \" + margin + \" V \" + (H - margin) + \" H \" + (W - margin) + \" V \" + margin + \" Z\");\n              marginRect.setAttribute(\"x\", margin); marginRect.setAttribute(\"y\", margin);\n              marginRect.setAttribute(\"width\", W - margin * 2); marginRect.setAttribute(\"height\", H - margin * 2);\n              marginRect.setAttribute(\"opacity\", margin > 0 ? 1 : 0);\n            }\n            drive(Math.round(parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.2\") * FPS), draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.2\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"comic-panels\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
